  "details": "I made an editor script which lets me dump a udon behaviour's public varaibles to json by using OdinSerializer.SerializationUtility.SerializeValue but this produces something that looks like json but upon closer inspection is invalid and does not parse using any regular json parser.\n\nI've attached an image that has 2 jsons:\n\n1. the output of the serialization function, with comments that show the invalid json\n\n2. how I would expect the output of the serialization function to look like, which is valid json\n\nThe main reason I think this would be useful because I prefer navigating json using a json viewer, but if it's not valid json then those tools do not work",
